Vocabulary Card Components
The atomic building blocks of the learning experience — every card type, state, and variant documented for development handoff.
COMPONENT LIBRARY
Word Card — Primary Learning Element
The Word Card is the most frequently used component in the app. It appears in lessons, reviews, quizzes, and the vocabulary browser. It must handle 7 distinct states and adapt to different exercise contexts.
STATES
Word Card States
Locked
New
Learning
Practicing
Gray background, lock icon, no text content visible. Opacity 0.5. Not interactive. Communicates "not yet available."
Blue border (2px, brand primary), "NEW" badge top-right, full image + word + translation. Subtle pulse animation on first appearance.
Standard card — image, English word, native translation, audio icon. White background, 14px corner radius, subtle shadow.
Reduced support — image smaller or hidden, translation shown only on tap. Tests active recall over passive recognition.
Reviewing
Mastered
Struggling
Minimal card — word only, no image unless requested. Clean typography-focused design. For spaced repetition sessions.
Compact card with green checkmark badge. Reduced visual weight. Appears in vocabulary browser and occasional review.
Amber border, support icon, extra visual aids enabled. More frequent appearance in sessions. Gentle "practice more" indicator.
PROPERTIES
Component Properties
Word Card Properties:

  state:        locked | new | learning | practicing | reviewing | mastered | struggling
  word:         string (English)
  translation:  string (native language)
  image:        ImageHash | null
  audio:        AudioRef
  phonetic:     string (IPA notation)
  confidence:   0-100 (drives state transitions)
  lastSeen:     timestamp
  context:      lesson | review | quiz | browser
  showImage:    boolean (overridable per exercise)
  showTranslation: boolean (overridable per exercise)
  isFlipped:    boolean (for flashcard mode)
  world:        string (thematic world the word belongs to)
