Wireframes & Layout Specifications
Low-fidelity structural layouts for every core screen. Mobile-first (390×844pt), focusing on hierarchy, content placement, and interaction zones.
PHASE 8
Wireframing Approach
Wireframes are structural blueprints — no color, no images, no typography styling. They answer: What content goes where? What's the hierarchy? Where does the user tap? They're fast to produce, fast to iterate, and force focus on layout over decoration.
WIREFRAME PRINCIPLES
Layout Guidelines
Mobile-First
Content Hierarchy
Gesture Zones
Safe Areas
All wireframes designed at 390×844pt (iPhone 14 viewport). Content hierarchy must work at this constraint before scaling up.
Every screen has one primary action, one secondary, and supporting content. Wireframes make this hierarchy explicit through size and position.
Thumb-reach mapping for one-handed use. Primary actions in bottom 40% of screen. Stretch targets (settings, profile) in top corners.
Respect iOS safe areas: 47pt top (status bar + notch), 34pt bottom (home indicator). Content padding: 24px horizontal minimum.
