Screen & Component Transitions
Every transition type documented with timing curves, duration, and implementation notes.
NAVIGATION TRANSITIONS
Screen-to-Screen Transitions
Tab Switch
Push Navigation
Modal / Bottom Sheet
Exercise Transition
Type: Crossfade
Duration: 200ms
Easing: ease-out
Behavior: Content fades while tab bar indicator slides. Previous screen fades out as new fades in. No lateral movement.
Type: Slide + Fade
Duration: 300ms
Easing: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1.0)
Behavior: New screen slides in from right. Previous screen shifts left 30% + fades to 0.7 opacity. Back reverses.
Type: Slide Up + Backdrop Fade
Duration: 350ms
Easing: spring(1, 80, 12)
Behavior: Sheet slides from bottom with spring physics. Backdrop fades to 50% black. Drag-to-dismiss supported.
Type: Slide + Scale
Duration: 250ms
Easing: ease-in-out
Behavior: Current exercise slides out left, new slides in from right. Brief 50ms gap with progress bar fill animation.
COMPONENT TRANSITIONS
In-Place State Changes
Card Flip (Word Card)
Button Press
Progress Bar Fill
Skeleton Loading
Type: 3D Y-axis rotation
Duration: 400ms
Easing: ease-in-out
Behavior: Card rotates 180° around vertical axis. Front fades at 90°, back appears. Scale dips to 0.95 at midpoint.
Type: Scale + Background
Duration: 100ms press, 200ms release
Easing: ease-out
Behavior: Scale to 0.96 on press. Background lightens/darkens 10%. Spring back on release.
Type: Width animation
Duration: 500ms
Easing: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)
Behavior: Slightly overshoots target width then settles. Green pulse ripple at fill point. Segment color change if applicable.
Type: Shimmer gradient sweep
Duration: 1500ms (loop)
Easing: linear
Behavior: Light gradient sweeps left-to-right continuously. Matches final content layout shapes. Fades to real content on load.
