Audio & Haptic Feedback
Multi-sensory feedback design — when and how sound and touch reinforce the learning experience.
SOUND DESIGN
Audio Feedback System
Correct Answer
Incorrect Answer
Word Pronunciation
Achievement Unlock
Sound: Bright ascending two-note chime (C5→E5)
Duration: 180ms
Volume: 60%
When: Immediately on correct answer selection
Note: Varies slightly each time (±2 semitones) to prevent fatigue
Sound: Soft descending single tone (Bb3)
Duration: 150ms
Volume: 40% (quieter than correct — less punitive)
When: On incorrect selection
Note: Gentle, not jarring. Think "oops" not "WRONG"
Sound: Native speaker recording
Duration: Variable (word length)
Volume: 80%
When: Auto-play on word card appearance, tap to replay
Note: Two speeds available — natural and slow
Sound: Ascending arpeggio (C4→E4→G4→C5) with shimmer
Duration: 600ms
Volume: 70%
When: Achievement modal appears
Note: Distinct from other sounds — celebratory, memorable
HAPTIC FEEDBACK
Touch Feedback Mapping
Haptic Feedback Map:

  Action                    Haptic Type          iOS API
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Button tap                Light impact         UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.light)
  Answer selection          Medium impact        UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.medium)
  Correct answer            Success notification  UINotificationFeedbackGenerator(.success)
  Incorrect answer          Error notification   UINotificationFeedbackGenerator(.error)
  Card flip                 Light impact         UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.light)
  Drag word chip            Selection changed    UISelectionFeedbackGenerator
  Drop word in place        Medium impact        UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.medium)
  Streak milestone          Heavy impact ×2      UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.heavy) ×2
  Level complete            Pattern: .-.-..      Custom pattern via CoreHaptics
  Pull to refresh           Light impact         UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.light)
  Swipe card (know/review)  Medium impact        UIImpactFeedbackGenerator(.medium)

  Rules:
    • Haptics always supplement, never replace visual/audio feedback
    • Respect system haptic settings (silent mode disables)
    • No haptics during passive content (reading, listening)
    • Maximum 3 haptic events per second to prevent numbness

