Validate every assumption with real users before committing to production. Test early, test often, test with the right people.
PHASE 11
Testing Philosophy
We don't test to confirm we're right — we test to find where we're wrong. Every round of testing should surface at least 3 things we need to change. If it doesn't, our test was too easy.
TESTING ROUNDS
Three-Round Testing Strategy
Round 1: Concept Validation
Round 2: Usability Testing
Round 3: Desirability Testing
Paper prototypes & clickable wireframes. Test with 5-8 target users. Questions: Does the learning model make sense? Is navigation intuitive? Do exercise types feel right?
Mid-fidelity prototypes. Test with 8-12 users across proficiency levels. Tasks: Complete onboarding, finish a lesson, review vocabulary, navigate between sections.
High-fidelity prototypes with motion. Test with 10-15 users for 1-week diary study. Measure: Daily return rate, session length, emotional response, NPS score.
SUCCESS METRICS
What We're Measuring
Task Completion Rate
Time to First Success
Session Return Rate
Error Recovery Time
Target: >90% for core flows (start lesson, complete exercise, check progress). Anything below 85% triggers a redesign.
Target: <2 min from app open to first correctly answered exercise. The "aha moment" must come fast.
Target: >60% Day 1 retention, >30% Day 7. Measures whether the app is compelling enough to come back to.
Target: <5 sec to recover from any error state. Users should never feel lost or stuck.

