AI Experience Specification
The detailed behavioral contract for every AI-powered feature — what the AI does, how it communicates, and what happens when it's wrong.
PHASE 13
Why AI Needs Its Own Phase
AI isn't a feature — it's a layer that touches everything. Without a dedicated specification, AI behavior becomes inconsistent, unpredictable, and untrustworthy. This phase defines the AI's personality, boundaries, and failure modes.
AI PERSONA
The AI Tutor Personality
Name & Identity
Voice & Tone
Boundaries
Error Handling
The AI tutor has no human name — it's "Context" itself. Not a character, not an avatar. An intelligent system that speaks naturally but never pretends to be human.
Encouraging but honest. "That was close! The word you're looking for is..." Never condescending. Never robotic. Adjusts formality to match learner's CEFR level.
AI stays in its lane: language learning. It doesn't give life advice, discuss politics, or pretend to have feelings. It redirects gracefully when asked off-topic questions.
When AI is uncertain, it says so. "I'm not sure about that pronunciation — let me play the reference audio." Transparency over false confidence.
AI FEATURES
AI-Powered Capabilities
Adaptive Difficulty
Conversation Partner
Pronunciation Coach
Content Generation
Real-time difficulty adjustment based on performance signals. Target: 75-85% success rate. Adjusts within a session, not just between sessions.
Free-form AI conversation that adapts vocabulary and grammar to the learner's level. Progressively challenges while maintaining comprehensibility.
Real-time phoneme analysis with visual feedback. Identifies specific sounds that need work. Generates targeted pronunciation exercises.
Dynamically generates sentences, stories, and exercises using the learner's known vocabulary. No two sessions are identical.

